      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @tsepez@chromium.org quick question:\n\nIf we have something like\n\n```int my_cool_variable \u003d 5;\nint pMyCoolVariable \u003d 10;```\n\nDo we currently guard against the case that `new_name` already exists as a variable somewhere in the file? Not sure if this would occur in the real codebase, so I just wanted to check.\n\nAgain, this would involve a very specific case where both a variable `pMyCoolVariable` and `my_cool_variable` both exist. I think it is unlikely to occur in the real codebase, but I wanted to check.",
      "range": {
